.TH QEMUSTYX 1
.SH NAME
qemustyx \- a whole Styx-over-the-radio run with no hardware in it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tools/radio/qemustyx.sh
.I qemu-system-arm
.RI [ kernel ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Two
.I qemu
guests run the station init over the modelled CC1120: one exports its
namespace and the other mounts it, over a connected AX.25 link, exactly
as the two clicker2 boards do.
.PP
Steps 5 and 6 of
.B doc/radio-plan.ms
had only ever been exercised on the bench, and that cost more than the
steps did.  A board stops answering a software reset and an arm cannot
be run until somebody presses a button; two boards are two serial
adapters and one wedges if anything opens the device twice; and every
reading arrives through a terminal's scrollback, which was returning a
frozen file for two runs in a row before
.I twoboard.session_for ()
was fixed.  None of that is about the radio.
.PP
.B tools/qemu-patches
models the part and gives it a socket back end, and
.B /lib/radio
already has an entry for each guest with a callsign, a peer and a role,
so the init runs unmodified.
.SH "WHAT IT CHECKS"
The two ends print different things, which is the point:
.B /lib/radio
makes
.B qemu2
the answerer and
.B qemu1
the caller, so the answerer must reach
.B ARMV7M-STYX-EXPORTING
and the caller
.BR ARMV7M-STYX-MOUNTED ,
and neither marker can be mistaken for the other.  A fault or a panic on
either console fails the run even when both markers appeared, because
the markers are printed before the traffic that follows them.
.PP
The answerer starts first, because it announces and waits; a caller
that calls before anything is listening gets
.B "ax25: no answer"
and that is a harness fault dressed as a link fault.
.PP
.B "The control is the second half:"
the answerer alone, with nobody to call it.  It must announce and never
export.  Without it an init that printed
.B EXPORTING
from a path not depending on a peer would pass \- which is the shape of
mistake that put two runs of a kernel that never booted into this
plan's notes.
.PP
Each guest's
.B "conf <name> (<kerndate>)"
line and its
.B "styx: ssl"
line are printed before any verdict, so a log says which image wrote it
and which arm it ran rather than leaving that to be remembered.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B OUTDIR
keeps both consoles in that directory instead of a temporary one.  The
verdict lines are a summary and the diagnosis is in what they leave out:
the run that found the keyring-plus-ssl arm failing reported only that
the answerer "did not export", when what mattered was the 22546 lines
after its last one.
.TP
.B SECS
how long the caller is given, default 90.
.TP
.B PORT
the loopback port for the radio back end, default 15723.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /lib/radio
.BR ssl= ,
.BR call= ,
.B peer=
and
.B role=
per board.
.B ssl=1
is set on the two qemu entries and not on the boards: the encrypted
arm's failures are link-level, and a guest pair has no air to lose
frames on, so it exercises devssl, the record reassembly and the memory
under a 109-byte frame without asking anything of the bench.
.SH EXAMPLES
The pair, and then the same with the keyring registered:
.IP
.EX
mk CONF=stm32f407 INIT=armv7mstyx istm32f407
tools/radio/qemustyx.sh $QEMU os/inferno/stm32f407/istm32f407
.EE
.SH "WHAT IT FOUND"
With
.B ssl=1
on the base conf the pair exports and mounts, and ssl costs 6536 bytes
of core \- 17680 free at export without it, 11144 with.
.PP
On
.B stm32f407auth
\- the same station with
.B $Keyring
registered \- the arm fails every time: both ends push
.B sha/rc4_256
and print
.BR ARMV7M-STYX-SSL ,
the caller reaches
.B MOUNTING
and puts 41 bytes on the air, the answerer receives them, and then the
answerer locks up before it exports.  One run printed
.B "no free Blocks"
22546 times, so the station has no Blocks left once ssl is pushed on a
conf that already costs 197K of text and a page.
.B "The flood is not the cause:"
with
.IR exhausted ()'s
print bounded the lockup happens with no message at all.  That arm wants
a bigger part, which is the same conclusion the identity half reached.
.SH SOURCE
.B tools/radio/qemustyx.sh
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IR ax25inittest (1),
.IR twostyx (1),
.IR radio (3),
.B doc/radio-plan.ms
